# Panel 260's R2 (provisional, author ratification pending): the platform
# layer's files are the runtime's own list, by their paths in its folder, never
# a name. A header of the program's own named `hero_util.h`, beside it, reaches
# nothing of the runtime: it is none of the layer's, so its group says nothing
# and the program builds and links none of the layer. Under the name rule the
# panel's route built first it was refused with a false sentence and a
# `certain` fix (the critic's `ownnamed`).
extern "hero_util.h"
    function util_answer() -> i64

function main()
    print(util_answer())
